{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791758350,"nonce":"mMje3Nk+9rGpci3N0rK7SIxNjs0=","message":"Ashui span constraint milestone 4bcdb95, under CSS/element umbrella 8780d6b, is completed locally in a02b6b8. This extends the existing TableColumns model from 8fbda23 / a960009: colspan content now contributes unbreakable and one-line widths to automatic columns. Shorter spans establish constraints before wider/overlapping spans, and missing widths are shared according to cached content preferences. Explicit pixel, percentage and star tracks retain their settings. Floating-point contributions are preserved; the last automatic track takes the remaining allocation.\n\nSpanning flows use the existing InlineFlow subscriptions and bounded layout passes. Span/column metadata and scratch arrays are cached; unchanged constraints skip template writes. Percentage spans observe their row width during active layout, so resizing releases or increases the automatic contribution without shaping text again. Row removal and owner disposal release listeners, including already-disposed cells.\n\nVerification: full tests/run.sh passed 932 checks, including 15 new TableSpans checks for overlapping constraints, span-only tables, fixed/percentage/star settings, width-only resizing, reactive text/font changes, removal, frame stability and cleanup. Existing Content and dark/light DataGallery were captured with tools/snapshot/run.sh and inspected directly: spanning cells and header/body/footer columns render correctly. Logs: .ashui/snapshots/table-spans-full-tests.log and table-spans-content/table-spans-data-*.log. No new native source or HDLL build was required; Cargo retains the actual pinned Git ABI.\n\nRowspan remains open and now has native prerequisite bcec1a0 in blinc_abi, associated with Ashui umbrella 8780d6b. Current independent row grids cannot place a cell across rows; the native layout and paint paths must support a shared row grid while preserving authored parents for CSS, focus, row hover and pointer bubbling. Background ordering must keep later row backgrounds below spanning cells. Components and slot assignment should remain on the language side. This prerequisite is recorded before implementation, without claiming rowspan support.\n\nOther remaining gaps include border-collapse/spacing and browser table display/layout modes, richer typography/display, generated-content host integration and the original umbrella's remaining CSS/element features. No code or git-bug refs were pushed; Ash was not modified.","files":null}]}